<PageTitle>Date & time — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Date & time" Category="Components"
                   ControlName="DatePickerControl · TimePickerControl · DateRangePickerControl · CalendarControl · TimeSpanPickerControl"
                   Tagline="Type it or pick it: dates with a calendar drop-down, times from a stepped list, ranges, multi-day selections and durations."
                   SourcePath="DatePickerControl.razor; TimePickerControl.razor; DateRangePickerControl.razor; CalendarControl.razor; TimeSpanPickerControl.razor">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>DatePickerControl</code> is a text box that parses what you type (sixteen built-in date formats, more with <code>ShowTime</code>) and opens a calendar
            on the 📅 button, F4 or Enter on an empty field. <code>TimePickerControl</code> is an editable drop-down of times from <code>Min</code>
            to <code>Max</code> every <code>Step</code>. <code>DateRangePickerControl</code> pairs two date pickers with a range calendar in a popup,
            and <code>CalendarControl</code> is that calendar on its own, in single, multiple or range mode. <code>TimeSpanPickerControl</code> is a
            row of number boxes for a duration. All five bind their value two ways and report validation through <code>EditContext</code> when
            used inside an <code>EditForm</code>.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="appointment" Title="Date, time and duration" RazorCode="@Code.Appointment" CSharpCode="@Code.AppointmentCs">
            <Description><p><code>MinDate</code> greys out the past; <code>ShowCalendarSidebar</code> adds Today, Tomorrow and week shortcuts to the drop-down. The time list runs 8:00 to 18:00 in half hours, and typed times outside it are refused with the control's own message. The duration commits when a box loses focus.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="fields">
                    <div class="field"><span class="field-label">Date</span><DatePickerControl @bind-Value="_date" MinDate="DateTime.Today" ShowCalendarSidebar="true" AriaLabel="Appointment date" /></div>
                    <div class="field"><span class="field-label">Start</span><TimePickerControl @bind-Value="_time" Min="@(new TimeOnly(8, 0))" Max="@(new TimeOnly(18, 0))" Width="150px" AriaLabel="Appointment time" /></div>
                    <div class="field"><span class="field-label">Duration</span><TimeSpanPickerControl @bind-Value="_duration" /></div>
                </div>
                <p class="result">@Appointment</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="range" Title="Date range" RazorCode="@Code.Range" CSharpCode="@Code.RangeCs">
            <Description><p>One <code>CalendarRange</code> binds both pickers and the popup calendar. <code>Min</code> and <code>Max</code> bound the travel window. Put the end before the start and the control reports it; the bound value still updates, so the page can refuse to count nights.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <DateRangePickerControl @bind-Value="_trip" Min="DateTime.Today" Max="DateTime.Today.AddDays(180)" AriaLabel="Trip dates" />
                <p class="result">@TripDates</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="calendar" Title="Calendar, several dates" RazorCode="@Code.Calendar" CSharpCode="@Code.CalendarCs">
            <Description><p><code>SelectionMode="Multiple"</code> toggles days into <code>Values</code>. <code>DisabledDate</code> greys out weekends, <code>FirstDayOfWeek</code> starts the grid on Monday, and the heading button switches to a year or decade view. Arrow keys move through the days.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="cal-row">
                    <CalendarControl @bind-Values="_departures" SelectionMode="CalendarSelectionMode.Multiple" Min="DateTime.Today" Max="DateTime.Today.AddDays(90)"
                                     DisabledDate="Weekend" FirstDayOfWeek="DayOfWeek.Monday" />
                    <p class="result departures">@Departures</p>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

