    <Accessibility>
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Keyboard" Title="Keyboard: date picker input" Rows="Vocab.DateKeys" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Keyboard" Title="Keyboard: calendar grid" Rows="Vocab.CalendarKeys" />
        <ul>
            <li>The date input carries <code>aria-label</code>, <code>aria-expanded</code> and <code>aria-invalid</code>; the 📅 button is named "Toggle calendar". A parse error renders in a <code>role="alert"</code> pill with <code>aria-live="assertive"</code>.</li>
            <li>The time picker's error and the range picker's error are <code>role="alert"</code>. The range picker is a <code>role="group"</code> whose inputs are named "Start date" and "End date".</li>
            <li>The calendar is a <code>role="grid"</code> with column headers and <code>aria-selected</code> cells. Each day is a button named with the full date; one day holds the Tab stop and the arrows move it.</li>
            <li>The time span boxes have no label beyond the unit letters d, h, m, s; put a visible label before the control.</li>
        </ul>
    </Accessibility>

